id: jf-707w
title: Expose Jellyfin 12 preview collection and query controls
description: "Migrate dedicated item methods from undocumented legacy user-scoped aliases to canonical Jellyfin routes and implement the additive 12.0-rc4 API surface: item-to-collection lookup, language filters, server-side person filters, activity-log filters/sorting, and playlist insertion position, while retaining read-only stable 10.11.11 behavior."
type: Plan
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[9]: agents,api,collections,filters,jellyfin-12,openapi,preview,read-only,toon
created_at: "2026-08-07T18:13:45.030Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T18:56:26.416Z"
assignee: codex-jellyfin-api-20260807
author: codex-jellyfin-api-20260807
estimated_minutes: 420
acceptance_criteria: "The GetItemCollections operation is available through a typed intuitive dedicated command with complete help and all output formats; New 12.0-rc4 item language, person, activity-log, and playlist position parameters are typed and exposed without changing stable defaults; Synthetic preview tests assert exact request contracts and structured outputs while compiled live 10.11.11 acceptance remains strictly read-only; Official-current docs, PM evidence, generated changelog, coverage, security, duplication, release, and review gates are recorded honestly"
definition_of_ready: "All-status PM inventory, duplicate scan, official releases, exact OpenAPI artifacts, local settings permissions, current branch, and live server version verified."
goal: jf-mqpo
value: Let humans and agents use the newest additive Jellyfin API capabilities without dropping stable-server safety.
impact: Closes the only preview-added endpoint gap and moves expensive client-side filtering to server-side typed requests where supported.
outcome: "A production-ready jf surface spanning stable 10.11.11 and opt-in Jellyfin 12 preview contracts, with no live mutation or private-data leakage."
why_now: Jellyfin 12.0-rc4 is the latest available preview and introduces new collection/query controls not represented by dedicated jf commands.
parent: jf-gn5j
reviewer: maintainer
risk: medium
confidence: high
sprint: jellyfin-12-preview
release: unreleased
