plan_mode: executing
plan_scope: "Typed dedicated CLI/API support for additive 12.0-rc4 operations and parameters, with stable-safe defaults, schemas, documentation, synthetic preview acceptance, and sanitized live 10.11.11 regression evidence."
plan_harness: codex
plan_resume_context: "Official 10.11.11 stable and 12.0-rc4 preview contracts verified; configured live server is 10.11.11. Implement only additive preview surfaces, never mutate live Jellyfin, and keep private artifacts under ~/.jellyfin-cli."
plan_validation[2]{text,command,expected}:
  Canonical PM-linked quality and live gate run,pm test jf-707w --run --progress with five measurements,All six linked commands pass; coverage shortfall remains measured against 100 percent; stable live contract reports zero full-scope unmatched tools and one version-unavailable preview command
  Draft PR published with PM links and full sanitized verification summary,gh pr create --draft --base main --head agent/jellyfin-12-preview-api-controls,"PR #55 exists with semantic title, no private details, non-publishing scope, exact gates, and durable main-branch PM links"
plan_decisions[2]{ts,author,decision,rationale,evidence}:
  "2026-08-07T18:14:03.638Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260807,Implement additive preview capabilities behind optional dedicated flags and commands while preserving stable request shapes when those options are omitted.,The configured production server is stable 10.11.11 and must not be mutated; additive optional controls can be verified synthetically against the exact preview contract without destabilizing current users.,"Official v10.11.11 and v12.0-rc4 releases plus exact OpenAPI compatibility summary: 1 added operation, 20 optional parameters, 25 removed operations."
  "2026-08-07T18:47:37.995Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260807,Represent OpenAPI enum arrays with exported literal unions and reject invalid activity/trailer sort values before network execution.,The preview contract defines sortBy and sortOrder as arrays of closed enums; stringly typed scalar forwarding would violate the exact request schema and defer actionable errors to the server.,"Official 12.0-rc4 ItemSortBy, ActivityLogSortBy, SortOrder, and LogLevel component schemas plus focused zero-request invalid-input tests."
plan_discoveries[2]{ts,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T18:14:03.255Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260807,"The 12.0-rc4 contract adds exactly one operation, GetItemCollections, and additive filters for Items, Trailers, Persons, ActivityLog, and playlist item insertion; it removes 25 legacy operations, which remain compatibility risks documented by schema diff."
  "2026-08-07T18:15:58.688Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260807,"Beyond the published additive diff, jf item methods depend on undocumented legacy /Users/{userId}/Items aliases. Official 10.11.11 and 12.0-rc4 both publish canonical userId-query routes; the 12 release removes legacy API route middleware, so canonical-route migration is required for real compatibility."
